(a) State two conditions for a real valued function \(f(x)\) of \(x\) to be a probability distribution of a discrete random variable. **(2 Marks)**

(b) Let \(X\) be a discrete random variable with probability distribution given by

$$
f(x) = \begin{cases} 
kx, & x = 1, 2, 3, 4 \\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

(i) Determine the value of the constant \(k\) **(2 Marks)**

(ii) Obtain the mean and variance of \((4X+1)\) **(2 Marks)**

(d) Let \(X\) be a continuous random variable with a probability distribution function given by

$$
f(x) = \begin{cases} 
2x, & 0 < x < 1 \\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Obtain the moment generating function of \(X\) **(3 Marks)**

(e) The probability density function of a continuous random variable is given by$$
f(x)=\begin{cases}
\sin x, & 0\leq x\leq \dfrac{\pi}{2}\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Obtain the median and mode of the random variable X. **(5 Marks)**

(f) 150,000 students appeared for an examination. The mean marks were 49 and the standard deviation of the marks was 6. Assuming the marks to be normally distributed, what proportion of students scored more than 55 marks? If in the same examination, grade A is to be given students scoring more than 70 marks, how many students will receive grade A? **(4 Marks)**

(g) X is a continuous random variable with p.d.f

$$
f(x)=\begin{cases}
\frac{1}{5}, & 0\leq x\leq 5\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Obtain the standardized random variable. **(4 Marks)**

a) A random variable X have a Poisson distribution given by

$$
f(x)=\begin{cases}
\dfrac{e^{-\theta}\theta^x}{x!}, & x=0,1,2,\dots\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Where the parameter $\theta$ satisfies $\theta>0$. Obtain the moment generating function of X, hence determine the mean and variance of X. **(10 Marks)**

A committee of three students is to be selected at random from a group of 10 applicants, of whom 6 are male and 4 are female. Let \(X\) denote the number of female students selected. Assuming that \(X\) follows a hypergeometric distribution, 

(i) find the mean and standard deviation of \(X\);
(ii) find the probability that no female students are selected.

-- ****

b) Let \(X\) be a discrete random variable with probability distribution given by


$$
f(x) = \begin{cases} 
 \frac{1}{5} & \text{for } x = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\
 0 & \text{otherwise}
 \end{cases}
$$

 Obtain the cumulative distribution function of the random variable \(X\), sketch its and find \(P(-3 < X < 3)\) **(6 Marks)**

-- ****

c) Let \(X\) be a continuous random variable whose probability distribution is given by


$$
f(x) = \begin{cases} 
 \frac{k}{x} &, 1 < x < 4 \\
 0 & \text{otherwise}
 \end{cases}
$$

 Show that the value of the constant \(k\) is \(2 \ln 2\). **(2 marks)**.



